SRC/strsch -- one change made for this collection=================================================bmgtest.c and bmgtest2.c (2026-09-18): UNIX FILE MODES ARE NOT OS-9 MODES.Both opened a named file with `open(name, 0)'.  On Unix that is O_RDONLY;on OS-9 mode 0 means NO ACCESS BITS AT ALL, so the open succeeds and everyread through the descriptor is refused.  What that looked like:    $ bmgtest beta f.txt        (nothing at all)    $ bmgtest beta < f.txt    beta-- a search that finds nothing in a file it can plainly see, and finds itat once on standard input.  Measured 2026-09-18.Both files now define BMG_RDONLY -- S_IREAD under OSK, 0 elsewhere -- anduse it.  Nothing else is touched.THIS IS A CLASS, NOT AN INCIDENT.  `patch' had the same fault in five places(SRC/patch/README.OSK), and it was found there first by the os9exec session,which traced `I$Open D0.b=$00' followed by `I$Read ... E_BMODE'.  A scan ofevery .c file under disk/SRC on 2026-09-18 found 76 non-comment call sitesof `open(x, 0)' or `creat(x, 0NNN)' across 34 source trees.  Most areharmless and some are deliberate:  * a stat() shim opens with mode 0 ON PURPOSE -- a GetStat needs no access    bits, and SRC/diff/os9.c says so in its own comment, "can't even open it    for NO access".  blarslib, smail, lua, eff_make and infoxpress all do    this and are right.  * several sites are inside `#ifdef MACOS' or `#ifdef VMS' and are never    compiled here -- unzip50/file_io.c is one.  * SRC/world/helper.c already has `#ifdef OSK ... open(Q1TEXT, 1)', so    somebody met this before and fixed that one.What is left is the list to work through: a mode-0 open whose descriptor isthen READ.  `agrep -f' was checked and works.  Still unchecked, each namedwith the line: adv/okplay.c:61 (reads /dd/GAMES/advmotd a byte at a time),trek73/save.c:215 (restoring a saved game), canfield/cfscores.c (the scorefile), cnews/appendfile.c:23, eff_bench/system.c:67, wish/files.c:166 anddvips/file_p.c:38.  The test is cheap: hand the program a NAMED file andgive it the same data on standard input.  If the second works and the firstdoes not, it is this.